    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'03Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 03.06.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2142$41 - 2019 iema;e\u00efn\u00be ui 24 jeks w\u00d5yrejdod - 2019'09'24No. 2142/41 - TUESDAY SEPTEMBER 24, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF MEMBER OF THE KATANA PRADESHIYASABHA UNDER SECTION 66A(1) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONS ORDINANCE(CHAPTER 262)\n\nWHEREAS the office of return member of Katana Pradeshiya Sabha has fallen vacant by reason of Death ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Leader of the Independent Group No. 1, to which Warnakulasooriya Sanath Rohan Fernandothe member belonged, was required by me under Section 66 A (1) of the aforesaid ordinance, to decide upon returnedmember of Independent Group No. 1 who belongs to such Independent Group and is not disqualified under Section 9 ofthe Local Authorities Elections Ordinance and who shall be declared selected as a member within a period of thirty (30)days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Leader of the aforesaid Independent Group No. 1 has communicated his decision to nominateMelani Rose Ferreira to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, Karunasingha Jayarathnage Sampath Madhawa, Returning Officer of the Katana PradeshiyaSabha, acting in terms of Section 66A(1) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) do hereby declarethat Melani Rose Ferreira was selected as the member of the Katana Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\nK. J. S. MADHAWA,Returning Officer,Katana Pradeshiya Sabha.District Election Office,Gampaha,24th September, 2019.\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT\n\nNotices under the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - G 30920\u2014 27 (09/2019)PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
