    "chunk_text": "III fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'09'25PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 25.09.20191A\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%hThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nw;s \u00fafYI EXTRAORDINARY\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nwxl 2142$59 \u2013 2019 iema;e\u00efn\u00be 25 jeks nodod \u2013 2019'09'25No. 2142/59 \u2013 WEDNESDAY, SEPTEMBER 25, 2019\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A \u2013 G 31089 \u2013 46 (09/2019)\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nORDER UNDER PROVISO (a) TO SECTION 38\n\nOrder No. 190 of 2019\n\nMy Ref. No.: 4-3/9/2018/IR/277-A.Sec. Ref No.: wkq/02/05/hdka Th.\n\nBY virtue of the powers vested in me by Proviso (a) of Section 38Land Acquisition Act, (Chapter 460) I, Gayantha Karunatilleke,Minister of Lands & Parliamentary Reforms do hereby direct theAcquiring Officer or any other officer authorized by him referred toin Columm 1 of the Schedule to take immediate possession of theland specified in the corresponding entry in Columm II of that Schedule.\n\nGayantha Karunatilleke,Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms.\n\nMinistry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d,Rajamalwatta Road,Battaramulla.18th September 2019.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n1. Land Acquiring Officer.\u2013 Divisional Secretary, KebathigoIIewa.\n\n2. Description of the land.\u2013 Allotments of land depicted in theAdvance Tracing No Aa/KBT/2018/1016, dated 31.12.2018 preparedby the Surveyor-General, situated in the Village called Wahalkada D8in the Grama Niladhari Divisions of No 41- Wahalkada in theDivisional Secretary' s division of Kebathigollewa in AnuradhapuraDistrict of North Central Province and bounded as follows.\n\n01. Lot No. 1 -WahalkadaYaya -Extent: About 0.0558 HectareNorth: Tracing No Aa/KBT/2018/1077; East: Lot No. 2; South:Lot No. 2; West: State Paddy Land."
