    "chunk_text": "wxl 2142$70 - 2019 iema;e\u00efn\u00be ui 26 jeks n%yiam;skaod - 2019'09'26\n\nNo. 2142/70 \u2013 THURSDAY, SEPTEMBER 26, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nNotice under Section 7\n\nMy Ref. No. :J/DS/2/9/4/03-2016.\n\nLand & Parliamentary Reforms Ministry Ref. No.: 4-3/9/\n\n2016/WS/520.\n\nI hereby give notice under Sub-section (1) of Section 7 of theLand Acquisition Act, as Amended by the Land Acquisition(Amendment) Act, No. 28 of 1964, that the Government intendsto acquire the following land/servitude which is required for apublic purpose:\n\nDescription of the Land to be Acquired:\n\nPreliminary Plan No.:- YA/JFF/2017/21-PPYA 2932 Village:- Vannarpannai South EastG.N. Division:- J/80 Grand Bazaar - Ward No. 17\n\n(New No. 15)D.S. Division:- JaffnaDistrict:- JaffnaProvince:- Northern ProvincePurpose:- To construct the Sewerage\n\nPumping Station 19\n\nG 31099 - 29 (2019/09)\n\nLot ExtentName of LandLand UseOwnerNo. Hectare\n\n10.0150Adiyarkunallankulam KannathiddyMunicipalalias KannathiddyTankCouncil,kulamJaffna.\n\nAll persons interested in the aforesaid land/lands on whicha servitude is to be acquired are hereby required to appearpersonally or by agent duly authorized in writing, before meat Divisional Secretariat, Jaffna on the 12th December 2019 at10.00 a.m. and are hereby requested to notify to me in writing(in duplicate) on or before the 18th November 2019 the natureof their interests in the land, the particulars of their claims forcompensation for the acquisition of the said land/servitude,the amount of compensation and the details of thecomputation of such amount.\n\nS.SUTHARSAN, Divisional Secretary,\n\nDivisional Secretariat, Jaffna.\n\nDivisional Secretatiat,Jaffna,19th September 2019.\n\n10 -372"
